      "text": "Anti-de Sitter space in four dimensions. Its version in two dimensions is the whole strip on which this wormhole stands, $L^2(-dt^2 + d\\sigma^2)/\\sin^2\\sigma$."
    },
    {
      "id": "bertotti_robinson",
      "kind": "family",
      "text": "Anti-de Sitter space of two dimensions times a sphere, the throat of an extreme charged black hole. Such a throat in global coordinates, joining two magnetically charged black holes, is the wormhole of Maldacena, Milekhin, and Popov in four dimensions [maldacena2023]."
    },
    {
      "id": "einstein_rosen_bridge",
      "kind": "family",
      "text": "The bridge of Einstein and Rosen, a wormhole that closes before light can cross it. Gao, Jafferis, and Wall made such a bridge traversable for a while by coupling its two sides [gao2017]."
    },
    {
      "id": "morris_thorne",
      "kind": "family",
      "text": "The traversable wormhole of Morris and Thorne, held open by exotic matter. In this wormhole the negative energy comes from quantum fields under a coupling of the two boundaries [maldacena2018]."
    },
    {
      "id": "near_horizon_extreme_kerr",
      "kind": "family",
      "text": "The throat of the extreme Kerr black hole, anti-de Sitter space of two dimensions with a deformed sphere twisted over it. The gravity of this wormhole, nearly anti-de Sitter gravity in two dimensions, approximates the dynamics of nearly extreme black holes [maldacena2018]."
    },
    {
      "id": "witten_black_hole",
